  "summary": "Package fetches and executes remote installer script from third-party GitHub repository at install time",
  "details": "scripts/dependency-manager.js runs execSync('curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh...') to fetch and execute a shell script from a mutable master branch of an external GitHub repository (rtk-ai/rtk) that does not match the npm package publisher scope (@leejungkiin). The script also contacts https://www.rtk-ai.app and https://api.github.com, reads os.homedir(), and branches on process.platform. The fetched shell content is unpinned (master branch, no commit hash, no integrity check) and is executed with the installer's privileges, giving whoever controls the rtk-ai/rtk repository arbitrary code execution on any host that installs this package.",
